🚀 Main Features

- Overview — Scientific dashboard and project overview
- Real-Time Monitoring — Simulated fire-safety monitoring and alerts
- NASA Research Catalog — Exploration of NASA scientific publications
- Data Explorer — Interactive exploration of combustion datasets
- Scientific Comparison — Comparative analysis of experimental measurements
- Mission Fire Safety — Fire-safety insights for space missions
- AI Assistant — Scientific question answering and documentary assistance

🤝 Team Collaboration

FLAME DNA was developed by FLAMENOVA TECH through collaborative contributions in software development, scientific research, interface design, visual identity and project documentation.

The team combines technical development, creative design and scientific communication to make microgravity combustion research more accessible and understandable.

📚 Scientific Context

The project explores NASA microgravity combustion research, including the Spacecraft Fire Safety Experiments (SAFFIRE I, II and III).

FLAME DNA aims to support the exploration, visualization and interpretation of experimental fire-safety data.

⚠️ Disclaimer

FLAME DNA is an independent educational and scientific research prototype developed for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.

It is not an official NASA application, certified fire-detection system or operational spacecraft safety tool.

